<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1900</h1><p class="ref-lede">1900 in world history: 28 events, 12 births, 13 deaths, 1 work, 7 states founded and 3 that came to an end. 842 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a><a href="/years/1897">1897</a><a href="/years/1898">1898</a><a href="/years/1899">1899</a><a href="/years/1900" aria-current="page">1900</a><a href="/years/1901">1901</a><a href="/years/1902">1902</a><a href="/years/1903">1903</a><a href="/years/1904">1904</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">John Hay promotes the Open Door Policy towards China</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">US Secretary of State John Hay pressed the great powers to grant equal trading rights in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and respect its territorial integrity. The Open Door became a cornerstone of American policy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-29">29 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The American League of baseball is organised</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Ban Johnson reorganised a minor league as the American League, with eight teams. It declared itself a major league in 1901 and met the National League in the first World Series in 1903.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-5">5 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Britain and the United States sign the first Hay-Pauncefote Treaty</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The agreement gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> the right to build a canal across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>. Rejected by the Senate, it was renegotiated in 1901, opening the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-27">27 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Labour Representation Committee founded in London</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Trade unionists and socialist societies formed a committee to elect working-class MPs. Renamed the Labour Party in 1906, it formed governments from 1924 and created the NHS in 1948.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-14">14 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Gold Standard Act puts the dollar on gold</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President McKinley signed the act fixing the dollar's value in gold and ending the long political fight over free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>. The US left the gold standard domestically in 1933.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-2">2 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">First Zeppelin airship flies over Lake Constance</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-von-zeppelin">Ferdinand von Zeppelin</a>'s LZ 1 made its maiden flight from a floating hangar on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a>. It was the first flight of a rigid airship, beginning an era that ended with the Hindenburg disaster of 1937.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/milan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/milan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-29">29 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">King Umberto I of Italy is assassinated at Monza</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The anarchist Gaetano Bresci shot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umberto-i">Umberto I</a> to avenge the killing of protesters in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> in 1898. It was one of a wave of anarchist assassinations that also claimed US President McKinley in 1901.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/beijing" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beijing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-14">14 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">International forces relieve the besieged legations in Beijing</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Troops of the Eight-Nation Alliance entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> and lifted the 55-day siege of the foreign legations by Boxers and Qing troops. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> was forced to pay a crushing indemnity.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-14">14 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Max Planck presents the quantum hypothesis</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Before the German Physical Society in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, Max Planck proposed that energy is emitted in discrete packets, or quanta. The idea, introduced to solve a problem in heat radiation, became the basis of quantum physics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/buganda-agreement">Buganda Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Buganda Agreement was signed on 10 March 1900 between Britain, represented by Sir Harry Johnston, and the regents of the young kabaka Daudi Chwa of Buganda, led by the chief minister Apolo Kagwa.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kousseri">Battle of Kousséri</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Kousséri was fought on 22 April 1900 near Kousséri, in present-day northern Cameroon, between French forces under Commandant Amédée-François Lamy and the army of the warlord Rabih az-Zubayr, ruler of Bornu.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-australia-constitution-act-1900" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-australia-constitution-act-1900.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-australia-constitution-act-1900">Commonwealth of Australia Constitution Act 1900</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Commonwealth of Australia Constitution Act 1900 is the British act, given royal assent on 9 July 1900, that united the six Australian colonies as the Commonwealth of Australia from 1 January 1901.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-golden-stool" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-golden-stool.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt · War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-golden-stool">War of the Golden Stool</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The War of the Golden Stool was an Ashanti uprising against British rule in 1900, also known as the Yaa Asantewaa War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-paardeberg" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-paardeberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-paardeberg">Battle of Paardeberg</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Paardeberg was fought from 18 to 27 February 1900 on the Modder River, in the Second Boer War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/french-conquest-of-bornu">French conquest of Bornu</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The French conquest of Bornu in 1900 followed the defeat and death of the warlord Rabih az-Zubayr, who had seized Bornu in 1893.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/foraker-act">Foraker Act</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Foraker Act was a United States law of April 1900 that set up civil government in Puerto Rico after the Spanish–American War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/toro-agreement">Toro Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Toro Agreement of 1900 was concluded between the British commissioner Sir Harry Johnston and the king and chiefs of Toro.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sannas-post">Battle of Sanna's Post</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Sanna's Post was fought on 31 March 1900 at the waterworks east of Bloemfontein, in the Second Boer War.</p></div></li></ol></section>
